# SilentLayer - workspace key
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` and replace the placeholder with your own secret:
#
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env        (PowerShell)
#   cp .env.example .env               (bash)
#
# WHAT THIS KEY IS
#   It is the fallback encryption key for images sealed WITHOUT a passphrase.
#   It is fed to HKDF-SHA-256, which derives the AES-256-GCM envelope key and
#   the scatter seed for the frequency layer.
#
# WHAT THIS KEY IS NOT
#   It is not a per-recipient secret. Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into
#   the shipped JavaScript, so anyone who can load this build can read the key
#   out of the bundle. Treat it as "keep casual visitors out of my own images",
#   not "protect images from the people I send them to".
#
#   For anything that leaves your own deployment, use the passphrase field in
#   the UI. That path uses PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256 with 310,000 iterations and a
#   random per-image salt, and the key never appears in the bundle.
#
# GENERATING A VALUE
#   Use a high-entropy random string, at least 32 bytes. Do not use a memorable
#   phrase: HKDF is a key-derivation function with no work factor, so a
#   human-guessable input is cheap to brute-force offline.
#
#     node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
#
# ROTATION
#   Changing this value makes every previously created passphrase-free image
#   unreadable. There is no key rotation and no escrow. Keep a backup.
#
# `.env` is git-ignored and must never be committed.

VITE_SILENTLAYER_WORKSPACE_KEY=replace-me-with-a-random-32-byte-secret
